			<div class="content" id="post-content-4680584">
									

<p>I'm very conflicted here. On one hand, it's a bit long, and I found myself skimming for quite a few parts. On the other hand, I really like SCPs that start off as some innocuous BS and eventually unfold into an epic story. In addition, it amuses me to no end that the Foundation has a protocol for receiving &quot;unexpected gifts&quot; from Groups of Interest.</p>
<p>&quot;Heh, gonna prank the Foundation by giving them a squirt gun that squirts lava! They won't be expecting this!&quot;</p>
<p>&#8230;</p>
<p>&quot;Hey, Jerry, we got another unmarked box&#8212;&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Put it in the scan chamber. Jesus Christ, it's the fifth time this week. Do these people have nothing better to do?&quot;</p>
<p>+1</p>

